<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! engine.filter.pages ~ a filter over the reader's view, its answer one bounded page

The filter language reads as TiddlyWiki's own: `[tag[memory]sort[title]]`, `[search[cursor]]`, `[prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]]`, `[has[status]!status[done]]`, and the link graph rides it too: `backlinks[]`, `links[]`, `transcludes[]`, `backtranscludes[]`. The filter computes over a reader's view of the wiki that holds only what this face may read, so no operator and no transclusion reads past the fence; `withheld` counts the matches that stay home (temp, state, custody titles) or rest in a bag this face holds no read on. The address stays a candidate until the operator reads the landing's list.

The answer reads {recipe, filter, titles, total, next, asOf}; name `fields` and each row carries them, {…, rows: [{title, fields}]} in place of `titles`. `collapse` reads the upcoming work skinny: each row carries `bytes`, and a meme root its `slots: [{slot, bytes, first}]`, the has-stack a skinny meme read answers, built by the same code, so one filter surveys many memes; unfold the one you need with a slot read.

`match` sweeps lines in one call: each row carries its record's matching lines, `lines: [{n, text}]` (a line past 512 bytes rides cut, `cut: true`), and `matches` counting every matching line, so a sweep (an L-Prime pass, a stale word) reads its matches with no read per title. Plain words match byte for byte; a `/source/flags` spelling reads as a regexp. `context` (0..8) carries that many lines around each match, touching windows merged; at most 64 lines a row, and a page past its byte cap sheds a row's tail lines and names `omitted: ["lines"]`. A record holding no text (a pointer) carries no lines. `context` without `match` refuses `filter-context-alone`. The filter narrows and the lens shows the lines: a search filter beside `match` hears one voice across every body of an entity.

The answer pages: at most 32 rows and `max-bytes` (65536 by default) per call; `total` counts every match and `next` names the cursor of the page behind: hand it back as `after` until `next` reads null (a terminal's `all` walks every page). A wiki that moved between pages refuses `filter-cursor-stale`; read again from the first page. A filter the engine cannot parse refuses `filter-malformed` with the engine's words.

A rendered tiddler's slice: where one read of the whole render (the record carrying `rendered-from`) answers more than you need, filter its sources for the slice, `[tag[road/rank]sort[order]]` with `fields` naming `text`. `recipe` names the wiki, and the filter runs in that wiki's own engine: `default` names the worn face's daemon wiki, a slug any wiki this face reaches; a wiki it reaches none of refuses `wiki-unreached`. A bag names no wiki and takes no filter (`wiki-not-anchored`): read a bag's record through the record read. `target` names another lit face this read visits, through its canon and working layer alone. A filter result carries the named wiki's words; turn it through the five tools.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ one-page · the-link-graph · the-work-skinny · hear-one-voice · a-visit

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`one-page` params=`filter/[tag[memory]sort[title]] recipe/default limit/5 ~ one page; after continues it, all walks it`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`the-link-graph` params=`filter/[[[[Room 4]backlinks[]]]] recipe/default ~ every record that links to Room 4`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`the-work-skinny` params=`filter/[prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/road/]] recipe/default collapse/true ~ each meme row skinny: its bytes and its slots`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`hear-one-voice` params=`filter/[[[all[tiddlers]search:text:literal[Lares (Stranger)]]]] match/[[Lares (Stranger)]] recipe/default ~ one persona heard across every body: the filter narrows, the lens shows the lines`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-visit` params=`filter/[tag[memory]] recipe/default target/h1 ~ a lit sibling's daemon wiki, read while you keep your own face`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ filter · recipe · bag · fields · collapse · match · context · limit · max-bytes · after · all · target · face

<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/face`>>

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`filter` params=`takes/filter needs/required seat/1 as/<filter> ~ a TiddlyWiki filter, run by the wiki's own engine`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`recipe` params=`takes/slug needs/required default/default ~ the wiki whose engine runs the filter; default names the worn face's daemon wiki`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/slug skins/cli ~ a bag names no wiki and takes no filter; it refuses wiki-not-anchored by name`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`fields` params=`takes/names ~ each row carries these fields`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`collapse` params=`~ each row answers its bytes, and a meme root its slots`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`match` params=`takes/words ~ each row carries its matching lines; a /source/flags spelling reads as a regexp`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`context` params=`takes/count ~ lines, 0 to 8, around each match, beside match`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`limit` params=`takes/count ~ rows per page; the ceiling of 32 holds`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`max-bytes` params=`takes/count ~ the byte cap on one page, 65536 by default`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`after` params=`takes/cursor ~ the page behind the cursor a prior answer named in next`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`all` params=`skins/cli ~ follow every cursor to the end`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`target` params=`takes/face ~ another lit face this read visits, by handle index or pet name`>>
```

